    "field": "Climate dynamics",
    "problem": "The drivers and physical mechanisms responsible for decadal-scale variations in Siberian warm season precipitation are poorly understood, with limited investigation into potential remote influences from major climate patterns like the Atlantic Multidecadal Variability.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a physical mechanism whereby North Atlantic warming (AMV) excites an eastward propagating wave train across Eurasia, which forms a dipole structure over Siberia, leading to anomalous southerly moisture transport and increased precipitation.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the remote influence of Atlantic multidecadal variability on Siberian warm season precipitation and to explain the underlying physical mechanism, involving an atmospheric wave train response, using observational data and numerical simulations.",
